-- title:
--   Eigenvectors in H¹ for points of the Taylor–Wiles Hecke ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, discretely valued, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with residue field $k$, let $S\subseteq\mathbb N$, let $N,r\ge 1$, let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$) — to $k$, let $q_1,\dots,q_t\ge1$ be natural numbers and $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_t\in k$, and put $L=N\bigl(\prod_j q_j\bigr)r$. Let $H\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ be a subgroup, and assume `OpComm` and `DiaComm`: the operators attached to the generators commute with one another and with the diamond operators $\langle u\rangle=$ `diamondL` for $u\in(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$. Let $F$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\mathcal O\to F$ injective, and let $\lambda$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from `HeckeRing N r qv S 𝒪 H θ α hc hdc` to $F$. Then there are a group homomorphism $e\colon(\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to F^\times$, scalars $\mu_1,\dots,\mu_t\in F$ and a nonzero $c$ in $H^1(L,H;F)=\operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(L)^{\mathrm{ab}},F)$ such that: for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ the transfer Hecke operator `heckeT` at $\ell$ sends $c$ to $\lambda(T_\ell)\,c$; for each $j$, `heckeT` at $q_j$ sends $c$ to $\mu_j\,c$; $\langle u\rangle c=e(u)\,c$ for all $u$; $e(u)=\lambda(\langle u\rangle)$ for $u$ in $H_r=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times\bigr)$; $e(u)=1$ for $u\in H$; and for each $j$ and each $a\in\mathcal O$ with residue $\alpha_j$ there is a monic polynomial $P\in\mathcal O[X]$ all of whose non-leading coefficients lie in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$ with $P(\mu_j-a)=0$.
--
--   This is the algebraic step, in the style of the Deligne–Serre eigenvector lemma, which turns an $F$-valued point of the Hecke ring acting on the localised first cohomology of $\Gamma_H(L)$ at a Taylor–Wiles level into a simultaneous eigenvector for the $T_\ell$, the $U_{q_j}$ and the diamond operators, with the extra information that each $U_{q_j}$-eigenvalue $\mu_j$ differs from a lift of $\alpha_j$ by an element satisfying an Eisenstein-type monic equation over $\mathcal O$. It is used by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_isEigenformWith_qCoeff_sub_mem_or_eisenstein_of_algHom`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.HeckeRing.exists_isEigenformWith_qCoeff_sub_mem_or_eisenstein_of_algHom), where, via Eichler–Shimura, such an eigenvector is matched with a weight-two eigenform with nebentypus on $\Gamma_1(L)$ or shown to be Eisenstein.
-- source:
